  "gloss": "encirclement; siege; surrounding",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "encirclement; siege; surrounding",
      "explanation": "The act of surrounding something or someone on all sides, whether in a military, police, or figurative context."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22408_houi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{敵|てき}を{包囲|ほうい}する。",
      "english": "To surround the enemy.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22408_houi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{警察|けいさつ}が{建物|たてもの}を{包囲|ほうい}した。",
      "english": "The police surrounded the building.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22408_houi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{城|しろ}は{三方|さんぽう}から{包囲|ほうい}され、{食料|しょくりょう}の{補給|ほきゅう}も{断|た}たれた。",
      "english": "The castle was besieged from three sides, and food supplies were also cut off.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {包|ほう} (wrap/enclose) and {囲|い} (surround). Describes the tactical or physical act of surrounding something. Common in military history, news reports about police operations, and figurative expressions about being cornered.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {包囲|ほうい}する: to surround, to besiege\n- {包囲|ほうい}{網|もう}: encirclement net, cordon\n- {包囲|ほうい}を{突破|とっぱ}する: to break through an encirclement\n- {包囲|ほうい}{攻撃|こうげき}: siege attack\n- {包囲|ほうい}される: to be surrounded\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {囲|かこ}む: to surround — the everyday verb for surrounding\n- {取|と}り{囲|かこ}む: to surround / to encircle — emphasizes closing in from all sides\n- {封鎖|ふうさ}: blockade — focuses on blocking access rather than surrounding\n\nNOTE ON HOMOPHONES:\nDo not confuse with {方位|ほうい} (compass direction/bearing), which has the same reading.",
